  "sourceReview": {
    "atomicity": "Lead transaction wrapper rolls required-write errors back. Override state/snapshot/audit all use that wrapper and caller connection. Convert project/Lead/links/copy audit/system snapshot also share a transaction, but convert fault cases are not among these14 actual groups.",
    "concurrency": "Lead and override store updates retain version predicates and zero-row results become Conflict409. Replacement updates old and pending records by separate CAS within one transaction, so the old weak-bulk path is removed.",
    "snapshots": "Latest system snapshot and semantic JSON comparison use formula/system score/rating and complete facts/gates; property order does not manufacture a system snapshot. Manual transition history remains independent.",
    "textAndDates": "Storable text check is applied to named persisted text fields, not arbitrary unknown fields/binary bytes. NUL/unpaired UTF16 reject400. Numeric18,2 precision is compared as text; business years1..9999 are explicit. This phase covers invalid inputs; complete positive boundary runtime cases remain outside these14.",
    "IProjection": "Summary emits a dedicated string[] view. Semantic no-op returns the existing record and performs no domain store update; session maintenance is separately handled.",
    "numberPool": "Create completes independent number reservation before acquiring the business TX; convert short preflight releases its connection, reserves, then rechecks convertibility in TX. This removes the observed nested pool acquisition shape.",
    "KClarifications": "Source now selects earliest full stored signed_at and sorts events by complete DateTime before ISO serialization; owner labels use available nonblank responsibility names/fallback. This is static coverage only, not certification of the pending full K matrix."
  },
